    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing across the entire monorepo. Let me summarize the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**Problem 1: Governance test failing with undefined `APPROVAL_STATUSES`**\n- The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from the governance module, but it was only available in the default export\n- **Fix:** Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES` and other schema constants in `/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n\n**Problem 2: Eval test failing with incorrect toxicity score**\n- The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving the references array as the `bannedTerms` parameter, causing it to flag all outputs as containing the reference phrases\n- **Fix:** Changed `toxicityMetric` to only accept the `outputs` parameter in `/packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`, so it uses the default banned terms and ignores the references passed by `runEvaluations`\n\nBoth fixes maintain backward compatibility and all existing public exports continue to work. The frai-core test suite now passes all 28 tests, and the entire monorepo test suite passes successfully.",
